    abstract actionLedgerRetention: Think.ActionLedgerRetention with get, set
    /// <summary>
    /// Lease window after which a durable <c>pending</c> action ledger row is assumed
    /// abandoned (its executor isolate died) and may be reclaimed and re-run.
    /// Reclaim re-runs <c>execute</c>, so it only applies to actions that declare an
    /// explicit <c>idempotencyKey</c> — that key is the developer's assertion that the
    /// keyed side effect is safe to retry. Fallback <c>tool:${toolCallId}</c> keys are
    /// never reclaimed. Set to <c>false</c> to disable stale-pending reclaim entirely
    /// (a stale row then blocks forever with <c>ActionPendingError</c>, the old
    /// behavior). This is a retry lease, not a retention window: retention answers
    /// "when may we delete old rows?"; the lease answers "when may we assume the
    /// previous executor died and retry safely?". Keep <c>actionLedgerRetention.pendingMs</c>
    /// well above this lease so reclaim happens before a sweep deletes the row.
