    /// <param name="callback">Streaming callback (typically an RpcTarget from the parent)</param>
    /// <param name="options">Optional chat options (e.g. AbortSignal)</param>
    abstract chat: userMessage: TurnInputMessages * callback: StreamCallback * ?options: ChatOptions -> JS.Promise<unit>
    /// <summary>
    /// Unified turn admission API (Turns RFC, step 2).
    /// <br /><br />
    /// Thin facade over Think.saveMessages, Think.continueLastTurn,
    /// Think.submitMessages, and Think.chat. Each <c>mode</c> delegates
    /// to the matching backing method with a narrowed option surface; the full
    /// unified superset lands with <c>_admitTurn</c> (step 3).
    /// <br /><br />
    /// - <c>mode: "wait"</c> (default) — blocking turn; returns TurnResult.
    /// - <c>mode: "submit"</c> — durable queued turn; returns SubmitMessagesResult.
    /// - <c>mode: "stream"</c> — RPC-style streaming; returns <c>Promise&lt;void&gt;</c>.
    /// <br /><br />
    /// <b>Re-entrancy.</b> Calling <c>mode: "wait"</c> or <c>continuation: true</c> from inside
    /// an active turn (a tool <c>execute</c>, a lifecycle hook) deadlocks on the turn
    /// queue — identical to calling Think.saveMessages or
    /// Think.continueLastTurn from there. Prefer <c>mode: "submit"</c> or
    /// Think.addMessages instead. Precise nested-call detection is deferred
    /// to <c>_admitTurn</c> (step 3).
    /// <br /><br />
    /// <b>Empty input (<c>wait</c>).</b> String, single-message, and array inputs that
    /// normalize to an empty list short-circuit to <c>{ status: "skipped" }</c> without
    /// running inference. A function <c>input</c> that resolves to <c>[]</c> at run time is
    /// not pre-checked (the function must see the in-queue transcript); step 3's
    /// <c>_admitTurn</c> centralizes empty-skip inside the queue.
    /// </summary>
    /// <remarks>@experimental</remarks>
    abstract runTurn: options: RunTurnWait -> JS.Promise<TurnResult>
